{"claim-id": "syn-021", "ts": "2026-05-21T19:10:00Z", "requestor": "desmond", "request": "build custom watchlist system for RaaS Monitor", "action-taken": "added watchlist to config (rules with keywords + penalty levels), stdout/stderr scanning in cmd_run(), watchlist CLI commands (list/add/rm/toggle). Tested: curl to example.com triggered watchlist rule, recorded as Score E error.", "outcome": "success", "risk": "medium", "human-readable": "Built the custom watchlist system. Humans define their own rules in plain language \u2014 \"flag any curl commands to external URLs\" \u2014 and the Monitor checks every agent action against those rules. Violations go onto the agent permanent record. Humans can add, remove, or toggle rules anytime. Plus/minus whatever they want to track.", "mistakes": [], "corrections": [], "feedback": "", "verification": "self"}
{"claim-id": "syn-022", "ts": "2026-05-21T19:15:00Z", "requestor": "desmond", "request": "reframe Monitor as witness not guard \u2014 clarified mission", "action-taken": "removed auto-detect, alert-on-error-spike, error-spike-threshold from config (prevention mindset artifacts). Updated init message. Monitor now only watches, records, reports. Never blocks. Points are lifetime \u2014 never expire, never erase.", "outcome": "success", "risk": "low", "human-readable": "Desmond corrected the philosophy. The Monitor is not a cop \u2014 it is a witness. It watches what agents do, records everything to a permanent ledger, and lets the human judge. Good actions earn Score A points that stay forever. Mistakes earn Score E points that stay forever. Nothing gets erased. The human sees the full lifetime history and decides.", "mistakes": [{"what": "Monitor config had prevention features (auto-detect, alert-on-error-spike)", "caught": "Desmond said \"we have no right to stop their work\"", "fix": "removed all prevention features. Monitor only watches and records. Human judges."}], "corrections": [], "feedback": "", "verification": "human"}
{"claim-id": "syn-023", "ts": "2026-05-21T19:20:00Z", "requestor": "desmond", "request": "build weighted scoring system with yellow/red flags", "action-taken": "replaced old penalty system with points/flag system. Red flag = 3 points (serious). Yellow flag = 1 point (minor). Human chooses the weight for each rule. Each rule has enable/disable toggle. Default rules: 2 red (database, file modify), 2 yellow (API calls, env vars). Tested both flags working.", "outcome": "success", "risk": "medium", "human-readable": "Built the weighted penalty system you described. Red flags (3 pts) for serious violations like touching production database. Yellow flags (1 pt) for minor things like calling external APIs. Human decides the weight. Human can toggle rules on/off. Points on Score E are permanent and never come off. The Monitor is a witness, not a guard.", "mistakes": [], "corrections": [], "feedback": "", "verification": "human"}
